    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d582-a1-a3">

                <pb facs="0702" n="660" xml:id="pg660"/>


                <head>Mr. Stanton to Mr. Chase.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">War Department,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington City, D. C.</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1863-05-19"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi>
                            19,1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to enclose herewith a copy
                    of an order of this department, designed to enforce the executive order of
                    November 21, 1862, against sundry persons engaged in purchasing horses and mules
                    for exportation.</p>
                <p>I would respectfully request the co-operation of your department.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>EDWIN M. STANTON, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of
                        War.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">S. P. Chase,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the Treasury.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
